Z||000005||StuGood||11-06-2000||11:05 PM||||All right... if your 1987 SE is original equipment (and it probably is), the car <B>has</B> no relays for the headlight doors.  Instead, it has an electronic HL door controller.  It's the black plastic thing you found in the LF fender, Haze.  The electronic controllers almost <B>never</B> quit; so says Ogre (I believe), and none of my controllers have ever failed.<P>The two big red wires going to the controller should have +12v all the time.  If not, then you probably blew a fusible link.<P>You can test each HL motor, by unplugging it from the harness, then manually cranking the HL halfway up.  <B>Briefly</B> connect a 12-volt source (battery charger) to the motor's 2 plug terminals.  The motor should run up or down.  Reverse polarity and the motor should run the opposite direction.     ||||reg||3
